Falsifies `jh7110_entropy::verification::neither_bit_set_is_always_not_ready`.

The defect: `generation_outcome` treats `SEED_DONE` as a second reason to read the register file, so a core
that has finished seeding but has produced nothing yet is read as `Ready` and yields whatever the
`RAND` registers last held.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(generation_outcome(status, interrupt_status, random_numbers), GenerationOutcome::NotReady)`: `SEED_DONE` alone now
produces `Ready`.

